{% block user %}Annotated each cluster in adata.obs['{{ params.get('groupby', 'leiden') }}'] by multi-model consensus over its top {{ params.get('n_top_markers', 25) }} marker genes; consensus labels and confidence are in adata.obs['cell_type'] and adata.obs['cell_type_confidence'].{% endblock %}

{% block methods %}Cell-type labels were assigned per cluster using a multi-LLM consensus annotation strategy [yang_mllmcelltype_2025]. For each cluster defined by adata.obs['{{ params.get('groupby', 'leiden') }}'], the top {{ params.get('n_top_markers', 25) }} marker genes were presented independently to two language models with species ('{{ params.get('species', 'human') }}') and tissue ('{{ params.get('tissue', 'unknown') }}') context. Agreement was quantified as a consensus proportion and Shannon entropy across model predictions, and each label was assigned a confidence tier (high / review / needs-expert). Labels lacking a resolved Cell Ontology identifier were flagged for expert review.{% endblock %}
